> Other Menus

DMS and SNAPS-OS have a variety of menus, here's an overview of them and how you can access them

## Runner
accessed with *SUPER+SPACE* or the button on the top left of the bar.

in apps mode, launch applications. in search mode, search /home directory.
plugins include settings search (start search with "?").

## Keybinds
accessed with *SUPER+K*

searchable overview of all keybinds from ~/.config/mango/binds.conf

## Clipboard History
accessed with *SUPER+V* or a bar widget

view clipboard history and load any entry back to clipboard

## Process List
accessed with *SUPER+X* or bar widgets

task manager: view, search and kill processes, monitor CPU/RAM/disk usage.
also shows system info (kernel, hostname, CPU, GPU).

## Dash
accessed through bar widgets

calendar, metrics, media player, wallpaper selector, weather and settings access

## Notifications
accessed with *SUPER+SHIFT+N*, notifications widget or control center

notification history, current notifications, do not disturb toggle, notification settings

## Control Center
accessed with *SUPER+ESCAPE* or bar widget

quick access to wifi, bluetooth, audio, theming, settings and power controls

## Power Menu
accessed with *SUPER+Z* or bar widget

reboot, shut down, sleep

## Notepad
toggled with *SUPER+N* or bar widget

simple space to keep quick notes

## Command Help
spawned with *SUPER+H*

searchable list of basic commands with TLDR overviews; enter opens the man page

## Full Help
this menu! spawned with *SUPER+SHIFT+H*

## Package Installer
spawned with *SUPER+Y* (shelly)

search pacman, AUR and optionally flatpak repositories

## Unipkg Installer
spawned with *SUPER+SHIFT+Y*

package-manager-agnostic TUI wrapper

## Mango Config Editor TUI
spawned with *SUPER+M*

list of mango config files with preview; enter opens in micro

## Mango Config Explainer TUI
spawned with *SUPER+ALT+M*

browse config files line by line with descriptions

## Layout Switcher
spawned with *SUPER+SHIFT+W*

switch between mangoWM layouts

## Wallpaper Switcher
spawned with *SUPER+W*

select wallpaper groups

## Bar Switcher
spawned with *SUPER+SHIFT+D*

switch bar layouts and toggle individual components

## Documentation
spawned with *SUPER+SHIFT+M*

quick access to reference lists and documentation links

## Project Selector
spawned with *SUPER+SHIFT+TAB*

browse and open git projects from ~/projects
